# What must not enter the build context.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters. The substrate's dependencies are installed inside
# the image from its own lockfile, and a local tree — built on whatever platform the person
# is sitting at — would be copied over them, so an image built on a Mac would carry that
# Mac's native binaries. It is also by far the largest thing here, and the context is sent
# to the daemon in full on every build.
#
# The suite and its support are excluded because the image carries the substrate rather
# than its tests. Nothing the entry point imports is under any of these.
#
# **`operator.ts` is deliberately not excluded**, even though nothing inside a sandbox runs
# it: it is declared in `bin`, and `npm link` creates a symbolic link for every name there
# whether or not the file exists. Excluding it would leave a dangling `jen-operator` in
# every agent's environment — a command that is present and cannot run, which is the exact
# shape the build check below exists to catch in the other entry point.
node_modules
**/*.test.ts
fixture.ts
gateway.ts
supervisor/harness.ts

# Neither of these is read from inside the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
